 # Order Packaging Geometry Feasibility for Drone Dimension Eligibility
 
+> [!warning] Disputed — Single-Zip width (252 mm vs 254 mm), flagged 2026-11-02
+> This page states that the current Single-Zip width limit is `254 mm` and that the 2026-07-30 value of `252 mm` is superseded, citing [[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/Zipline Payload Dimensions Slide - Week of 2026-09-07|Zipline Payload Dimensions Slide - Week of 2026-09-07]]. That source note does not support this reading: its Envelope card reads `338 × 252 × 205 mm`, it describes the 3D render's `10 in / 254 mm` label as a rounded-imperial pairing, and it says "Do not treat `254 mm` as a superseding envelope width." The only vault artifact showing `254 mm` is the 3D render label. Every other vault source, including sources dated after the slide ([[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/PRD/Drone Eligibility Check - MVP Plan - 2026-09-17|Drone Eligibility Check - MVP Plan - 2026-09-17]], [[Wonder/Wonder Fulfillment/Projects/1P Drone Delivery/Raw/Investigation - Cookbook Weight and Dimension Backfill Review - 2026-10-26|Cookbook Weight and Dimension Backfill Review - 2026-10-26]]), uses `252 mm`. The width figures on this page are left as written pending human resolution; see `.knowlery/freshness/notes/zipline-single-zip-width-252-vs-254.json`.
+
 ## Executive Conclusion
 
 The per-container dimension resolution approach — resolve Cart items into packaging SKUs, look up each SKU's length/width/height, then 3D bin-pack against the Zipline envelope — **is not viable**, and the blocker is not data completeness.
